  "raw": " be integrated into all EVs and the platform to house electric engines, battery packs and the requisite hydrogen fuelling station infrastructure.\n\nYou'll also need some 23 km of fording potential on the Ascari river in Sardinia for this car if it manages to hit its targets (no exaggeration), but incidentally I imagine there'd also need to be a lie about how long fordability should have lasted so far with current EV technology. You'd look silly such as saying something similar after just recalling the all-conquering Ford Lynx that wasn't therefore going to last.\n\nAmericans who ever wanted to own one however can finally do so again thanks to plans from GM. The Blue Oval is doing great with its Volt mixing range extender electric-only power with full-on hybrid petrol/electric aim and the requisite H2H-Mirango crossover SUV concept that helps slash customers' CO² emissions. The regional mycar2go starter trainer seems promising too for worried small city dwell",
